{
  "id": "COMPOUND:22173 - PROTEIN:5866",
  "verbalization": "Cyclotetracosane appears to have a shared target relationship with NCI-H446 through multiple pathways. The first pathway links Cyclotetracosane to Raji cells, which are targeted by Diosmetin 7-O-Beta-D-Glucopyranosyl-(1->2)-Beta-D-Glucopyranosyl-(1->2)-[Alpha-L-Rhamnopyranosyl-(1->6)]-Beta-D-Glucopyranoside, which in turn targets NCI-H446. The second pathway connects Cyclotetracosane to Hepatocytes, which are targeted by Licochalcone D, and Thelephantin K, which also targets NCI-H446. These findings suggest that Cyclotetracosane may act on hepatic or cellular targets that are involved in the regulation of NCI-H446, potentially through a common mechanism of action or pathway. The evidence supports a role for Cyclotetracosane in modulating cellular processes that influence NCI-H446, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
